\subsection{Language Modeling}\label{app:language-modeling}

\subsubsection{Experimental setup}\label{app:lm-experimental-setup}
We follow the same basic training setup as in~\citep{grazzi-iclr25a}. We use the training pipeline \texttt{flame} from the flash-linear-attention~\citep{yang2024fla} repository. All of our models are trained on NVIDIA L40s or NVIDIA A100 40GB or NVIDIA H100 94GB GPUs. We used 16 to 32 GPUs at a time to train one model, in a 2 to 8 node setup, depending on resource availability. We used DeepSpeed with ZeRO-2~\citep{rajbhandari2020zero} for distributed training. All models were trained with an effective batch size of $524\,288$ tokens, and a learning rate of 3e-4. We optimized the models with AdamW~\citep{loshchilov-iclr19a} ($0.01$ weight decay) and used cosine annealing~\citep{loshchilov-iclr17a} for the learning rate schedule with linear warm up for 512 steps. We used a total of 10\,500 GPU hours to train all of our models. 

