A discussion of the search algorithms is beyond the scope of this paper, but we focus here on different cost models for evaluating a point in the search space.  \textit{Performance models} can be used to compute a metric associated with each point, with the algorithm selecting a code variant associated with the best value of the metric.   Alternatively, \textit{autotuning}
is frequently used to measure the execution time of an optimized code variant running on a specific hardware platform.  A third option is to build a \textit{predictive model} that derives a schedule using deep learning: a learning phase typically derives an associated cost with different schedules and inputs, and inference performs a lookup into the model at runtime.  
