\subsection{Example 6: Nonsmooth function with conic constraints}

This example introduces the application of the \pkg{CEopt} solver to an optimization problem involving a nonsmooth function subject to conic constraints, marking the first instance in this series where constraints are explicitly considered. The objective function and constraints are formulated to test the solver's efficacy in handling lake of differentiability and complex constraint boundaries, characteristics typical of many real-world optimization problems.


