\subsection{System Overview}\label{system}
%\vspace{-1.5mm}
Polaris's compute capacity is 560 nodes, composed of 280 ProLiant XL645d Gen10 Plus dual-node systems. Each node contains a 32-core 2.8 GHz AMD Epyc 7543P ``Milan'' CPU, 512 GB system RAM, and four NVIDIA A100 SXM4 40GB GPUs. Nodes communicate over an HPE Slingshot 11 fabric, with each node connected by dual 200 Gb/s Cassini-based NICs. The fabric is a 40-group dragonfly topology with 14 nodes per group. 
