In this work, we presented a systematic approach for co-analyzing diverse telemetry data collected from a production system, uncovering key patterns in workload characterization and their GPU resource usage. 
%The result is a summary dataset, compressed by 94\%.
%To the best of our knowledge, this is the first study to provide an in-depth analysis of modern HPC workloads in terms of their GPU resource and power demands.
%this is  the first study co-analyzing job scheduling and GPU power telemetry data collected from production system.
Through in-depth statistical analysis, we identified notable relationships between workload characteristics and GPU resource demands, including GPU cores, GPU memory, and GPU power.
Given these insights, we then highlighted practical opportunities for applying power savings strategies.   
We anticipate these insights will guide HPC researchers seeking to optimize energy efficiency.  

Future work includes domain analysis to investigate how scientific fields correlate with workload and power characteristics, as well as extending this analysis to additional supercomputing systems.

