Figure~\ref{fig:fingerprint_variation} shows how the performance of our Fuzzy Fingerprint framework on the \textit{Friends} and \textit{Big Bang Theory} datasets varies with the size of the fuzzy fingerprint (i.e., the top-$k$ hidden units retained from the last hidden layer). 
As we increase $k$, the accuracy rapidly improves and approaches the score achieved by the fully fine-tuned RoBERTa model (which leverages all 768 units in its last hidden layer). Notably, beyond $k \approx 150$, the FFP curve saturates slightly below RoBERTa, indicating that retaining only a fraction of the hidden units is sufficient to achieve nearly the same level of accuracy as using all 768 dimensions.

