Another interesting benefit of the fuzzy fingerprint representation is its direct interpretability. By maintaining class-specific fuzzy fingerprints, we can measure a sample’s similarity to each class fuzzy fingerprint using Equation \ref{eq:similarity}. 
This property of fuzzy fingerprints enables analyzing how a given sample’s fuzzy fingerprint aligns (or fails to align) with a specific speaker's fuzzy fingerprint, revealing when the model is most uncertain. 
In such cases, the utterance might be considered generic, meaning it lacks strong stylistic cues and could plausibly belong to multiple speakers.


